<title>UK: Royal Brunei to fly ex-London daily Dec 2.</title>
<headline>Royal Brunei to fly ex-London daily Dec 2.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Brunei Airlines is starting daily services from London Heathrow to the Middle and Far East from December 2, the airline said in a statement here.</p>
<p>The new service will use Boeing 767-300ER adding 10,000 kilos of cargo capacity each week.</p>
<p>The flights from Heathrow will fly via Abu Dhabi on Mondays with an additonal stop at Rangoon on Tuesdays and Friday. On Wednesdays and Sunday flights will just stop at Dubai but will also land at Singapore on Thursdays and Saturdays. -- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
